As I've shown you before, you too can
trace your origins back to ancient Egypt.

135
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:20,989
All right, that is enough.

136
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:22,800
I know who I am.

137
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:27,360
I'm a far better duelist than you,
and I plan to win this tournament.

138
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:32,228
Regardless of what you and your
demented brother may believe,

139
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,140
You made two mistakes.

140
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,820
The first was handing Obelisk to me.

141
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,981
The second was expecting it back.

142
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,340
That card is mine.

143
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:44,120
And soon I'll possess the
other two Egyptian God cards.

144
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:48,889
Then I'll have the world's most powerful
deck, and you can do a favor for me.

145
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:52,800
Take your Hocus Pocus nonsense
to someone else's tournament,

146
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:56,040
because to me, it's a
colossal waste of time.

147
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,760
Let's go, Roland.

148
00:07:57,940 --> 00:08:00,400
Begin this duel at once. Yes, sir.

149
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,020
Begin now!

150
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:09,320
My Millennium Necklace predicts that
Kaiba's lack of faith will be his downfall.

151
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,420
I'll go first.

152
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:15,517
I don't need a magic trick
to predict your demise.

153
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:18,720
So I will summon the mighty Force Raider.

154
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,240
Now he'll place a card face down.

155
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:27,240
And now I'll place one card face down.

156
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,077
That ends my turn.

157
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,220
Kaiba,

158
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,897
the power of my Millennium
Necklace shall predict

159
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:35,800
